    "body": "`nvim_buf_set_lines()` on an unloaded buffer whose `BufReadCmd` autocmd deletes that buffer reads the freed `buf_T` (heap-use-after-free in `normalize_index`). A testing tool found this; it does not come from a real plugin or config.\n\n```lua\nlocal a=vim.api\nlocal b=vim.fn.bufadd('cancelled.txt')\na.nvim_create_autocmd('BufReadCmd',{buffer=b,once=true,callback=function()\n  a.nvim_buf_delete(b,{force=true})\nend})\nprint(pcall(a.nvim_buf_set_lines,b,0,-1,true,{'replacement'}))\n```\n\nSave the script as `reduced.lua` and run, with an ASan build:\n\n```\nnvim --headless -u NONE -i NONE -n -l reduced.lua\n```\n\nOutput:\n\n```\nError in BufReadCmd Autocommands for \"<buffer=2>\":\nE813: Cannot close autocmd window\nE813: Cannot close autocmd window\n==645==ERROR: AddressSanitizer: heap-use-after-free on address 0x527000003908\nREAD of size 4 at 0x527000003908 thread T0\n    #0 in normalize_index src/nvim/api/private/helpers.c:452\n    #1 in nvim_buf_set_lines src/nvim/api/buffer.c:339\n    #2 in nlua_api_nvim_buf_set_lines build/src/nvim/auto/lua_api_c_bindings.generated.h:615\nfreed by thread T0 here:\n    #2 in apply_autocmds_group src/nvim/autocmd.c:1823\n    #4 in readfile src/nvim/fileio.c:314\n    #5 in open_buffer src/nvim/buffer.c:334\n    #6 in buf_ensure_loaded src/nvim/buffer.c:234\n    #7 in api_buf_ensure_loaded src/nvim/api/buffer.c:60\n```\n\nI expected `nvim_buf_set_lines()` to fail with an error, as the release build does, rather than touch a buffer that no longer exists.\n\nIt reproduces at 0851e7dabed9 (latest upstream when checked). The ASan build aborts with the report above. The normal (release) build exits with rc 0, prints the E813 messages and `false Failed to insert line`, so nothing is visible without a sanitizer.\n\nLooks like `buf_ensure_loaded` (buffer.c) returns success after `open_buffer` even though the autocmd wiped the buffer, and `api_buf_ensure_loaded` (api/buffer.c) then returns the dangling pointer; a `buf_valid()`/loaded re-check there might be enough. Open PR #37373 touches nearby code in api/buffer.c and may be related; I did not test it here.\n\nI can send a patch if that helps.\n\nFound with an LLM-based testing tool; I used Claude to reduce it and look for the cause.\n",
